.TH FOREST-LOCKER 1 "October 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-locker \- Forest idle and session lock daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-locker
.RB [ \-\-no\-logind ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-locker
dims the screen, turns displays off and locks the session after the idle
timeouts configured under Lock Screen in
.BR forest-settings (1)
(stored in
.IR ~/.config/Forest/Locker.conf ).
It locks by running
.BR forest-lockscreen (1),
and restarts it if it crashes while the session should be locked.
.PP
It also locks on logind's
.B Lock
signal (e.g.
.BR "loginctl lock-session" )
and before suspend, and provides the
.B org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
service so applications can inhibit idle or request a lock.
.PP
It is started by
.BR forest-session (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-logind
Don't talk to logind: no lock or sleep signals, and no locked/idle hints.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest-lockscreen (1),
.BR forest-session (1)
